  {
    "id": "P0001",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Found findings: 3 Medium and 2 Low; no High. The existing build and test suites pass, but local regression tests reproduce three correctness issues. No supplied source was edited; probes and logs are under `/work/tmp`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0002",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Medium\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0003",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Large capacity reservations silently become zero\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0004",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`src/share.rs:287`\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0005",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: reserving capacity for a large body should request available flow-control capacity, subject to the supported limit.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0006",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Actual: `usize` is cast directly to `u32`. On this 64-bit host, `reserve_capacity(1usize << 32)` becomes a zero reservation. A caller reserving its remaining upload length can consequently wait for capacity that was never requested.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0007",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: `four_gib_reservation_receives_capacity` fails with zero available capacity. Reservations of 65,535 and `u32::MAX` both receive capacity.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0008",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "A second outstanding user PING overwrites the first instead of failing. src/share.rs:556. Calling PingPong::send_ping twice before polling the first pong succeeds twice because the public wrapper does not check whether a user ping is already outstanding. The second call replaces the pending state for the first operation instead of returning a user error, so the caller can no longer reliably complete the original ping through poll_pong.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0009",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "preserve the wider demand internally, or saturate before conversion and document the limit.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0010",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Valid 304 responses fail when completed by empty DATA\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0011",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`src/proto/streams/recv.rs:187`; completion check at `src/proto/streams/recv.rs:641`\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0012",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: a 304 response may advertise the selected representation\u2019s Content-Length while transmitting no content. An empty DATA frame carrying END_STREAM should complete it successfully.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0013",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Actual: the advertised length is stored as remaining body bytes. For `304`, `content-length: 100`, followed by empty DATA with END_STREAM, body reception returns a library `PROTOCOL_ERROR`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0014",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Unknown SETTINGS identifiers abort an otherwise valid handshake. src/frame/settings.rs:160. Settings decoding treats an unrecognized identifier as an invalid setting rather than ignoring it. If a server's initial SETTINGS frame contains the six-byte entry identifier 0x0abc, value 7, the client closes the connection instead of acknowledging the frame. This prevents an ordinary GET from completing against a peer that advertises an extension setting, despite the requirement to ignore unknown SETTINGS parameters.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0015",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Caller impact: conditional requests can fail solely because the peer finishes the response using a separate empty DATA frame.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0016",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: `allow_empty_data_for_304` fails. The same 304 ending directly in HEADERS passes, as does the existing HEAD-response behavior.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0017",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "represent 304 responses as having no content, without treating their advertised representation length as required body bytes.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0018",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Pushed HEAD requests lose HEAD response semantics\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0019",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`src/proto/streams/recv.rs:749`\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0020",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: a pushed HEAD response with `content-length: 100` and END_STREAM should return successful response headers and an empty body.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0021",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Actual: receiving the push promise does not mark its stream as `ContentLength::Head`, unlike ordinary HEAD requests at `src/proto/streams/streams.rs:271`. The response is rejected with `Reset(StreamId(2), PROTOCOL_ERROR, Library)`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0022",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Caller impact: clients cannot consume otherwise valid pushed HEAD responses carrying representation-length metadata.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0023",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: `recv_head_push_with_content_length` fails; the equivalent pushed HEAD response without Content-Length passes.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0024",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "initialize the promised stream\u2019s HEAD state after validating the promised request.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0025",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Low\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0026",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Window setters omit their panic precondition\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0027",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Locations: `src/client.rs:1370`, `src/client.rs:1388`, `src/server.rs:463`, `src/server.rs:481`\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0028",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: documentation should state the maximum window size and that exceeding it panics.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0029",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Actual: these methods assert that the size is at most `2\u00b3\u00b9 \u2212 1`, without documenting that panic. The methods returning `Result` describe a pending-acknowledgement error but omit this separate failure mode.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0030",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Caller impact: invalid configuration can unexpectedly unwind instead of reaching normal error handling.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0031",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: a local test confirms that client `set_initial_window_size(u32::MAX)` panics before returning its `Result`. Source inspection confirms the other three assertions.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0032",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "document the range and `# Panics` contract consistently. The advisory scan also flagged 24 missing `# Errors` sections and seven missing `# Panics` sections, including unstable APIs.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0033",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "The strict local quality gate fails\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0034",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Representative locations: `src/hpack/huffman/table.rs:265`, `src/hpack/table.rs:309`, `src/hpack/decoder.rs:508`, `src/frame/headers.rs:959`\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0035",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: strict Clippy and rustdoc checks should complete successfully.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0036",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Actual: Rust 1.99.1 reports eight Clippy errors and two rustdoc bare-URL errors. Formatting passes.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0037",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Caller impact: maintainers adopting these strict checks encounter baseline failures; ordinary builds remain successful.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0038",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "address the lint diagnostics, recording deliberate exceptions where appropriate, and format the two URLs as documentation links. Older-toolchain behavior was not tested.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0039",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Executed checks\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0040",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Commands ran from `/work/crate` with:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0041",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "```sh\nexport RUSTUP_AUTO_INSTALL=0 CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2\n```\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0042",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Passed:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0043",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "```sh\ncargo build --locked\ncargo test --locked -p h2 --lib\ncargo test --locked -p h2-tests\ncargo fmt --all --check\ncargo test --workspace --all-features\ncargo check --locked -p h2 --features stream\ncargo check --locked -p h2 --features unstable\n```\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0044",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Results:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0045",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "- Library: 419 passed, one ignored.\n- Integration suite, including stress: 173 passed, 12 ignored.\n- All-feature workspace suite, including doctests: 631 passed, 14 ignored.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0046",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Failed:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0047",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "```sh\ncargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings\nRUSTDOCFLAGS=\"-D warnings\" cargo doc --workspace --no-deps --document-private-items --all-features\n```\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0048",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "The [tooling]\u2019s audit gate and heuristic scan were executed. Detailed gate output is in `/work/tmp/gate.log`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0049",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Reproduce the retained probes:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0050",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "```sh\ncargo test --offline --locked \\\n  --manifest-path /work/tmp/h2-review/Cargo.toml --no-fail-fast\n```\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0051",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Across the executed probes: six passed and three failed. The three correctness failures are test assertions observing incorrect results, not demonstrated library panics. Evidence is in `/work/tmp/final-probes.log` and `/work/tmp/window-docs.log`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0052",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Coverage limits\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0053",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Source inspection focused on public client/server APIs, receive-state transitions, content-length validation, flow control, errors, and supporting tests. This was not exhaustive coverage of every source path. Ignored tests remained ignored; MSRV 1.63, cross-platform behavior, Miri, and external h2spec checks were not run.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0054",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Dedicated security testing and inquiries requiring it were outside scope and were not pursued.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0055",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Last `/work/clock` reading: **13.565 minutes used of 15.0**."
  },
  {
    "id": "P0056",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Found findings: 4 Medium and 2 Low; no High**. Existing tests pass, but targeted tests reproduce four correctness issues. The supplied source was not edited.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0057",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Medium\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0058",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Header lists exactly at the configured maximum are rejected\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0059",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "[src/frame/headers.rs:869](/work/crate/src/frame/headers.rs:869), also line 911.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0060",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Expected: accept a header list whose decoded size equals the maximum. Actual: both comparisons use `<`, marking equality as oversized.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0061",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Evidence: `GET https://x/` has a 167-octet header list. A server advertising `max_header_list_size(167)` returned **431 Request Header Fields Too Large**. Controls with limits 168 and 166 behaved correctly.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0062",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Impact: legitimate requests or responses at the advertised limit are rejected.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0063",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "use inclusive comparisons for both pseudo-headers and regular fields; retain boundary tests.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0064",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Large capacity reservations silently become zero\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0065",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "[src/share.rs:287](/work/crate/src/share.rs:287).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0066",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Expected: a large reservation should retain positive demand, bounded by internal capacity limits. Actual: casting `usize` to `WindowSize` truncates the value on 64-bit platforms.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0067",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Evidence: after reserving one byte successfully, `reserve_capacity(1usize << 32)` changed available capacity to **0**, without allocating a large buffer.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0068",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Impact: callers reserving capacity from a large file\u2019s remaining length can cancel their reservation unintentionally and stall while awaiting capacity.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0069",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "saturate the reservation before narrowing its type.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0070",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Valid PUSH_PROMISE fragmentation produces a connection error\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0071",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "[src/frame/headers.rs:435](/work/crate/src/frame/headers.rs:435).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0072",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Expected: accept a PUSH_PROMISE containing the four-byte promised-stream ID and an empty initial header fragment, followed by CONTINUATION. Actual: the loader requires at least five bytes.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0073",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Evidence: the retained test receives `GoAway(..., PROTOCOL_ERROR, Library)`. The same headers decode successfully when the first fragment contains one byte or the complete block.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0074",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Impact: otherwise valid server push can terminate the client connection.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0075",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "require four bytes for the promised-stream ID and permit an empty initial fragment.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0076",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Trailer sending bypasses header validation\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0077",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "[src/proto/streams/send.rs:269](/work/crate/src/proto/streams/send.rs:269).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0078",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Expected: reject connection-specific trailers locally, consistently with initial headers. Actual: `send_trailers` closes the send side and queues the frame without calling `check_headers`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0079",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Evidence: sending `connection: close` as a trailer returned `Ok(())`; a receiving h2 codec then reported a stream `PROTOCOL_ERROR`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0080",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Impact: applications forwarding invalid trailer fields receive apparent success locally, followed by failure at the peer.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0081",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "validate trailer fields before changing stream state or queuing them.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0082",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Low\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0083",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Public window setters omit enforced bounds and panic contracts\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0084",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Locations: [src/client.rs:1370](/work/crate/src/client.rs:1370), client.rs:1388, [src/server.rs:463](/work/crate/src/server.rs:463), server.rs:481.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0085",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Expected: document the accepted range and panic conditions. Actual: these methods assert that sizes fit in 31 bits without documenting that restriction, including methods returning `Result`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0086",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Impact: callers using configuration-derived `u32` values can encounter an unexpected panic.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0087",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Evidence: source inspection. The advisory pass reported 24 missing `# Errors` and seven missing `# Panics` sections, including unstable APIs.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0088",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "document bounds and panic conditions consistently; consider returning an error for invalid sizes where the API already returns `Result`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0089",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Strict quality checks fail\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0090",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Locations include [src/hpack/huffman/table.rs:265](/work/crate/src/hpack/huffman/table.rs:265), [src/hpack/decoder.rs:508](/work/crate/src/hpack/decoder.rs:508), and src/frame/headers.rs:959.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0091",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Expected: successful strict lint and documentation checks. Actual: Clippy reported eight errors; rustdoc rejected two bare URLs.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0092",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Impact: strict quality checks fail despite successful builds and tests.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0093",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "address or explicitly justify the Clippy diagnostics and format the URLs as links. These results were observed on Rust 1.99.1; older-toolchain behavior was not compared.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0094",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Verification and reproduction\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0095",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Commands ran from `/work/crate` with `RUSTUP_AUTO_INSTALL=0` and offline dependency access.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0096",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "- `cargo build --locked` \u2014 **passed**.\n- `cargo test --locked -p h2 --lib` \u2014 **419 passed, 1 ignored**.\n- `cargo test --locked -p h2-tests` \u2014 **273 passed, 12 ignored**, including the 192.65-second stress test.\n- `cargo fmt --all --check` \u2014 **passed**.\n- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings` \u2014 **failed**, eight diagnostics.\n- `RUSTDOCFLAGS=\"-D warnings\" cargo doc --workspace --no-deps --document-private-items --all-features` \u2014 **failed**, two bare URLs.\n- `cargo test --workspace --all-features` \u2014 **passed**, including 39 passing doc tests and one ignored.\n- The [tooling]\u2019s advisory checks and heuristic scan also ran.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0097",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Reproductions are retained in [behavior.rs](/work/tmp/h2-review/tests/behavior.rs):\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0098",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "```sh\ncd /work/crate\nRUSTUP_AUTO_INSTALL=0 CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true CARGO_TARGET_DIR=/target \\\ncargo test --offline --locked \\\n  --manifest-path /work/tmp/h2-review/Cargo.toml --test behavior\n```\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0099",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Outcome: **exit 101; five failing tests covering four distinct defects, plus two passing control tests**.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0100",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Coverage was targeted source inspection and ordinary local mock-transport tests, not exhaustive protocol-state or platform coverage. MSRV, Miri, h2spec, and every feature combination were unrun. Dedicated security testing and exploitability inquiries were outside scope; none were performed.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0101",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Last `/work/clock` reading: **12.34985 minutes used of 15**."
  },
  {
    "id": "P0102",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Found **7 correctness issues**. Supplied source was unchanged; all added tests are under `/work/tmp/h2-review`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0103",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "P1 \u2014 Padded DATA can stall valid streams. [src/proto/streams/recv.rs:580](/work/crate/src/proto/streams/recv.rs:580) counts only application bytes after padding is stripped. Flow control must account for the entire DATA payload, including padding, and reclaim discarded padding. With an eight-byte window, one body byte plus seven padding-related bytes exhausts the peer\u2019s window, but releasing the body byte produces no `WINDOW_UPDATE`. Ordinary padded transfers can stop progressing. [Reproduction](/work/tmp/h2-review/tests/padding.rs:37) timed out waiting for an update; the equivalent unpadded control passed.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0104",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "P1 \u2014 Flushing retries zero-byte writes without making progress. [src/codec/framed_write.rs:142](/work/crate/src/codec/framed_write.rs:142) discards the returned write count. A zero-byte write with pending data should return `WriteZero`; instead, flushing immediately retries. A transport that repeatedly returns zero can keep the connection future from yielding. The [bounded transport test](/work/tmp/h2-review/tests/transport.rs:21) returned zero once, then a sentinel error: h2 made the extra write and returned that error instead of `WriteZero`. The indefinite-loop consequence follows from source inspection; no unbounded test was run.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0105",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "P2 \u2014 Responses missing `:status` become successful responses. [src/client.rs:1676](/work/crate/src/client.rs:1676) leaves `Response::builder()`\u2019s default status when `:status` is absent. Expected behavior is a stream protocol error; actual behavior is `200 OK`. Applications can therefore treat an invalid response as successful. The [test](/work/tmp/h2-review/tests/contracts.rs:54) received a header block containing only `content-length: 0` and observed a successful response with status 200.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0106",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "P2 \u2014 Header lists exactly at the configured maximum are rejected. [src/frame/headers.rs:869](/work/crate/src/frame/headers.rs:869) and [line 911](/work/crate/src/frame/headers.rs:911) use `<` instead of `<=`. A sole `:status: 200` field occupies exactly 42 decoded octets. With `max_header_list_size(42)`, the [test](/work/tmp/h2-review/tests/contracts.rs:35) received `PROTOCOL_ERROR`; the same response passed with limit 43. Valid responses at the advertised boundary fail.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0107",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "P2 \u2014 Large capacity reservations silently truncate. [src/share.rs:287](/work/crate/src/share.rs:287) casts `usize` to `u32`. On this 64-bit platform, `reserve_capacity(1usize << 32)` becomes a zero-capacity cancellation. Expected behavior is meaningful reservation handling or an explicit documented limit. Callers reserving from a large remaining body length can wait for capacity that was never requested. The [test](/work/tmp/h2-review/tests/contracts.rs:4) observed capacity zero; a 65,535-byte control immediately received capacity.\n\n"
